<!--
  <sui-radio-group> — SUI port of <ship-radio-group>.
  Manages selection across <sui-radio> children with roving tabindex and
  arrow-key navigation. Participates in forms via a light-DOM hidden input.

  Prop parity vs <ship-radio-group>
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  value (string, '')          ✓ reflect — selected radio value
  disabled (bool, false)      ✓ reflect — disables all radios
  tone (Tone, 'default')      ✓ reflect — propagated to radios
  size (sm|md|lg, 'md')       ✓ reflect — propagated to radios
  name (string, '')           ✓ — form field name
  label (string, '')          ✓ — aria-label for the group
  required (bool, false)      ✓ reflect — sets aria-required on host
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Events: ship-change → sui-change { detail: { value } }
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  Slots: (default) — sui-radio children
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

  NEW SURFACE (re-port from feat/next, parity-gate pass)
  ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
  - No tone channels or per-component `theme` blocks existed here (the
    group only sets a `tone` prop and propagates it to children; tone IS
    the global channel on each child, no per-component redeclaration
    was in scope). No change to the tone story on this component.
  - The `:host([hidden]) { display: none }` rule is dropped — framework
    BASE_CSS owns [hidden]. The `color: var(foreground)` is also
    owned by BASE_CSS (the framework host default). What stays in
    style is genuinely component-specific: a vertical flex column with
    a space-2 gap (a host-level layout; <column> is for INNER elements,
    the host has no <column> primitive, so this is a one-rule
    `style` override of the framework's block default) and a font-
    family declaration (no font-family prop in the sx vocabulary).
  - The `value` prop is declared via the legacy `prop` tag (not the
    `component` block): the block's string-default-literal arm does
    not add reflect (only unions / bools do), and the controller
    writes to this signal in onSelect / onNav — without reflect the
    host attribute wouldn't mirror the change and downstream tests
    (which query `el.getAttribute('value')` after a click) would fail.
    The other props ride the `component` block fine (unions + bool
    auto-add reflect; the read-only string props don't need it).
-->

<prop name="value" type="string" default="" reflect />
<component>{
  props: {
    disabled: false,
    tone: 'default' | 'primary' | 'info' | 'success' | 'warning' | 'destructive' | 'accent' | 'muted',
    size: 'sm' | 'md' | 'lg',
    name: '',
    label: '',
    required: false,
  },
}</component>

<style>
  /* host layout: vertical flex stack (the inner <column> primitive is
     for element children, not the host; this is the one host-level
     layout this component needs). */
  :host {
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    gap: var(--space-2);
    font-family: var(--font-body);
  }
</style>

<slot></slot>
